.TH PRIVATE-VM 1 "2026-07-19" "private-vm 0.0.0-dev" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
private-vm \- orchestrate disposable role-isolated NixOS virtual machines
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B private-vm
[global options] COMMAND [command options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B private-vm
is the unprivileged client for the root-owned
.BR private-vmd (8)
service. It creates no intentional persistent plaintext session state. It is
not an anonymity system, a perfect-erasure mechanism, or proof that scanned
content is safe.
.PP
Run
.B private-vm --help
for the complete command tree and
.B private-vm COMMAND --help
for command-specific options.
.SH IMPORTANT COMMANDS
.TP
.B doctor --strict
Perform read-only compatibility and installation checks.
.TP
.B system install --dry-run
Show every mutation proposed by the generic Linux installer.
.TP
.B system install --accept
Apply the exact reviewed generic-install plan as root.
.TP
.B system uninstall --dry-run
Show removable package-managed paths while preserving configuration, image
cache, enrolled-device state and user exports.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/private-vm/config.toml
Root-owned, non-secret daemon configuration.
.TP
.I /run/private-vm/control.sock
Unix-domain daemon control socket. No TCP fallback exists.
.TP
.I /var/lib/private-vm/images
Verified persistent image cache, preserved by uninstall.
.TP
.I /var/lib/private-vm/scratch
Encrypted ephemeral ciphertext only; it is not a user-data directory.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 2 usage; 10 through 24 documented operational failures; 70 internal
failure. See the installed documentation or project CLI reference for the exact
stable mapping.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR private-vmd (8),
https://github.com/StevenBuglione/private-vm/blob/main/docs/07-cli-reference.md,
https://github.com/StevenBuglione/private-vm/blob/main/docs/22-installation.md
